record lege-ecosystem.observation.layout-model-eval-20261108/1 : observation {
    title "Layout models measured 2026-11-08: RF-DETR-S beats PP-DocLayout-M, trails PP-DocLayout-L; Lege's 0.35 threshold drops real text; PP-L cannot load in lege-gpu"
    state verified
    scope [
        path "lege-gpu/src/vision/**",
        path "lege-process/models/**",
        path "lege-process/pipeline/**"
    ]
    statement """
        On the teacher-labelled dev_auto (544 pages) and regression (88 pages) splits and the 28 globalhistory dev pages, AP50 and every under-detection metric rank PP-DocLayout-L > RF-DETR-S > PP-DocLayout-M (dev_auto AP50 at 0.20: 0.785 / 0.695 / 0.576; RF-DETR-S clips text 2-3x less than either PP model). RF-DETR-S scores are calibrated lower than PP-M's: at Lege's production confidence_threshold 0.35 its missed-text rate is 4x the 0.20 figure (dev_auto 2.5% vs 0.6%) and the two globalhistory misses (dust jacket p0006, time chart p0533) are detected at 0.20. PP-DocLayout-L's paddle2onnx export (3 inputs, in-graph NMS) is rejected by lege-gpu (Range, BatchNormalization, Clip, Floor, GatherND, Log, Mod); it was measured through onnxruntime only. Vulkan latency 1x3x640x640: RF-DETR-S 32.7 ms, PP-M 22.0 ms. lege-gpu's decode agrees with onnxruntime on globalhistory page 7; in Lege, text regions inside a detected image region are carved away, so a page detected as a full-page image keeps no text regions with any model. No human-verified (gold) page has been scored: the 180 dev and 130 test gold pages are still pre-filled. Details: dev-notes/lege-process/layout-model-eval-20261108.md.
        """
    observed_at git:9c0b9fe352a41e5c84536e27507ebc80b5f6889c
    method command
    watches [
        "lege-process/models/*.onnx",
        "lege-process/pipeline/config.rs",
        "lege-gpu/src/vision/decode/picodet.rs"
    ]
    review_after 2027-02-08
    author "dk"
}

record lege-ecosystem.observation.layout-model-v2-benchmark-20261110/1 : observation {
    title "Layout model v2 (RF-DETR-S, 70k hand-corrected set) measured against v1 on 2026-11-10 and placed in lege-process/models (uncommitted)"
    state verified
    scope [ path "lege-process/models/**" ]
    statement """
        RF-DETR-S v2 was trained from the COCO-pretrained small checkpoint (not from v1) for 6 epochs at 640, batch 16, on 64,785 pages of 547 books from the 70k set (DocLayout-YOLO prefill, PP-DocLayout-L labels for abandon boxes, bulk fixes, 16,090 pages reviewed by hand). Colab A100, two sessions because Colab ended the first after about 2 h 10 min; about 20.7 compute units. Validation EMA mAP50:95 by epoch: 0.598, 0.611, 0.631, 0.634, 0.629, 0.645 (final epoch exported; ONNX parity with PyTorch exact).

        Measured with train/eval_layout.py (Lege decode, threshold 0.20) on pages reviewed by hand from books neither model trained on, v1 -> v2 (v2 = the shipped fp16 file with toc, reference and formula rows of the class map zeroed):
        - dev, 928 pages of 20 books: AP50 0.678 -> 0.739; AP50:95 0.547 -> 0.667; text coverage 0.976 -> 0.986; clipped text 24.1% -> 7.7%; missed text 0.7% -> 0.4%; over-merged 4.4% -> 6.1%; false text area 8.8% -> 5.7%; figure AP50 0.961 -> 0.979.
        - final test, 514 pages of 22 books: AP50 0.800 -> 0.845; AP50:95 0.689 -> 0.789; text coverage 0.986 -> 0.988; clipped text 17.8% -> 3.8%; missed text 0.5% -> 0.5%; over-merged 2.9% -> 2.2%; false text area 3.2% -> 1.6%; figure AP50 0.962 -> 0.973.

        On v1's pseudo-labelled sets v2 has lower AP and less clipped text: regression (88 pages) AP50 0.835 -> 0.703, AP50:95 0.776 -> 0.597, clipped 11.7% -> 9.0%, missed 1.9% -> 0.5%; dev_auto (544) AP50 0.697 -> 0.576, AP50:95 0.618 -> 0.471, clipped 7.7% -> 5.3%. The AP drop is the classes v2's training set lacks (toc 2 boxes, reference 150, formula 1,489 of 543,104) and running_footer conventions; the owner decided those classes are not needed and they are no longer emitted.

        fp16 storage plus the zeroed rows changed no metric by more than 0.004 on the reviewed sets. The file (57,844,974 bytes, sha256 d83ea9e29c1b7945f9ae...) replaced lege-process/models/layout-rfdetr-s.onnx in the working tree; not committed and lege was not rebuilt. Loaded through LEGE_DATA_DIR by the 2026-11-08 release lege.exe it ran Structures pp. 191-200 without error on Vulkan with tensor-core GEMM. On those ten pages v2 reports 2 header and 8 paragraph_title where v1 reports 6 header and 4 paragraph_title, and no page number where v1 found 1.

        Method notes: PNG was rejected for the training bundle after measurement (599 KB and 7.4 ms decode a page against 222 KB and 3.8 ms for JPEG q92 4:4:4 at long side 1024). Details: google-colab-work/layout-detection RUNBOOK.md (v2 run), DATASET-V2.md sections 16-19, eval/v2/*.json.
        """
    observed_at git:f11fee2e0ef3c3f95c03307ef8305fe2879b2a4b
    method command
    watches [
        "lege-process/models/layout-rfdetr-s.onnx",
        "lege-process/models/layout-rfdetr-s.md"
    ]
    derived_from [
        @lege-ecosystem.decision.rfdetr-book-layout-model-replaces-doclayout-m,
        @lege-ecosystem.observation.layout-model-eval-20261108
    ]
    author "dk"
}

record lege-ecosystem.observation.ocr-v5-v6-recipe-20260820/1 : observation {
    title "PP-OCRv6 TensorRT improved the recipe-PDF proxy over embedded v5"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "lege-document-ocr/**", path "lege-ocr/**" ]
    statement """
        On the two-page D:\to-sort\5-Minute Hummus Recipe - NYT Cooking.pdf at 300 DPI capped to 12 MP and forced OCR, embedded PP-OCRv5/WGPU scored 17.88% CER and 19.16% WER against the pipeline's native text extraction, while PP-OCRv6-tiny/TensorRT scored 12.00% CER and 14.17% WER. The native v6 worker passed detector and recognizer inference after cold engine compilation. A generic Paddle/WGPU v6 model pack passed checksum validation but failed detector construction, so it is not a viable v6 replacement yet.
        """
    observed_at git:3f520cc03211e48adaa77c1da9bc639c53d2d351
    method command
    watches [ "lege-document-ocr/**", "lege-ocr/**", "lege-gpu/**" ]
    derived_from [ @lege-ecosystem.work.ocr-backend-scheduler/4 ]
    verified_by [ @lege-ecosystem.evidence.ocr-v5-v6-recipe-20260820/1 ]
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

