record lege-ecosystem.observation.old-layout-corrections-hurt-model-v2-20261110/1 : observation {
    title "Through Lege, the PP-DocLayout-M corrections made layout model v2 worse; without them AP50 rises from 0.486 to 0.663 on 882 reviewed pages"
    state verified
    scope [ path "lege-process/core/engine_impl.rs", path "lege-process/models/**" ]
    statement """
        Lege's own detections (LEGE_BBOX_TRACE `planned raw` lines: model v2, threshold 0.20, two-pass NMS, then post-processing) were scored against 882 hand-reviewed pages of ten held-out dev books with train/eval_lege_trace.py (google-colab-work/layout-detection), once with a debug-fast build that still had layout_correct and once with it removed.

        With the corrections -> without: AP50 0.486 -> 0.663; AP50:95 0.363 -> 0.598; text AP50 0.527 -> 0.863; caption AP50 0.139 -> 0.743; heading AP50 0.494 -> 0.655; running_header AP50 0.668 -> 0.958; page_number AP50 0.707 -> 0.970; figure AP50 0.969 -> 0.969; table 0.797 -> 0.797. Over-merged text 24.4% -> 3.6%; false text area 10.7% -> 3.7%; clipped text 10.2% -> 9.2%; text coverage 0.970 -> 0.967; missed text 2.8% -> 3.1%. Of 1,034 ground-truth running headers, footers and page numbers: found as furniture 810 -> 1,003, found as text 5 -> 15, not found 219 -> 16 (with the corrections, widened text boxes swallowed them). Of 585 running headers alone, 9 (1.5%) come out as text without the corrections. Headings found 403 -> 428 of 504; none came out as furniture.

        Full-page figure expansion (page_analysis) only ran on Linux and was not part of either arm on Windows. The comparison was run on Windows with --no-ocr; text detections dropped from 2,474 to 2,277 boxes, the difference being the synthetic text boxes.
        """
    observed_at git:8ceb9c292119c66c22632a3e580eeb7d5cfa4217
    method command
    watches [ "lege-process/core/engine_impl.rs", "lege-process/models/layout-rfdetr-s.onnx" ]
    derived_from [ @lege-ecosystem.observation.layout-model-v2-benchmark-20261110 ]
    author "dk"
}

record lege-ecosystem.observation.ppocrv6-wgpu-blockers-resolved-20260822/1 : observation {
    title "PP-OCRv6 on wgpu was blocked by four concrete gaps, all now closed"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "lege-gpu/**", path "lege-ocr/**", path "lege-process/scripts/**" ]
    statement """
        The earlier finding that a Paddle/WGPU v6 model pack "failed detector construction" had four independent causes, each now fixed. (1) Stock Paddle exports name the graph input `x`, which match_target in lege-gpu/src/vision/onnx/load.rs bound to the paddle-rotate target's fixed 224x224 contract; the v5 assets had been renamed to pp_det_image/pp_rec_image out of band and that recipe was never committed. (2) lege-gpu had no Erf kernel (v6 builds GELU from it, 13x in det, 10-13x in rec); added as UnaryKind::Erf with an Abramowitz-Stegun 7.1.26 WGSL shader and a matching CPU reference. (3) v6 det uses ConvTranspose 2x2/stride-2 and v6 rec keeps BatchNormalization behind a Squeeze; both are rewritten at prep time, ConvTranspose into Conv1x1+DepthToSpace (exact for kernel==stride, zero pad) and BN into Mul+Add. (4) MaxPool/AveragePool rejected auto_pad!=NOTSET and ignored it during shape inference, so PP-OCRv6's stride-1 SAME_UPPER 2x2 windows shrank the feature map by one pixel and surfaced as a Concat axis-2 mismatch; both now resolve auto_pad exactly as Conv already did. Whole-spatial ReduceMean(axes=[2,3]) is also rewritten to GlobalAveragePool at prep. The v6 small dictionary (18708 glyphs) is a near-superset of v5's 18383 - 35 dropped, 360 added - and repairs v5's Latin-1 coverage, which held only 70 of 192 codepoints in U+00C0..U+017F.
        """
    observed_at git:3f520cc03211e48adaa77c1da9bc639c53d2d351
    method command
    watches [
        "lege-gpu/src/vision/onnx/**",
        "lege-gpu/src/vision/decode/db.rs",
        "lege-ocr/assets/**",
        "lege-process/scripts/prepare_ppocr_models.py"
    ]
    supersedes [ @lege-ecosystem.observation.ocr-v5-v6-recipe-20260820/1 ]
    verified_by [ @lege-ecosystem.evidence.ppocrv6-wgpu-embedded-20260822/1 ]
}

