record lege-ecosystem.observation.truetyping-halftone-review-20260905/1 : observation {
    title "TrueTyping and JBIG2 halftone review with diagnostic reproductions"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Reviewed TrueTyping and JBIG2 halftoning at 4a7349f9. Reproduced low-range halftone corruption in native and jbig2dec decoders, partial-cell ink loss, default dictionary tone bias, oversized TrueTyping component loss, malformed contour counts from a 380px connected grid, O/0 semantic collision, and GUI reflow/halftone incompatibility. Additional code findings concern blanket OCR fallback suppression, highlight clipping, and inert/misleading halftone controls. Full findings, priorities, evidence, limitations and quality experiments: docs/reviews/truetyping-halftone-20260905.md. Existing tests passed: 26 glyphfont tests and 7 halftone decoder tests. No application fixes made.
        """
    observed_at git:4a7349f94b1fb6f6f90b871be5dbb9b5736062de
    method instrumented
    watches [
